  "name": "HCV RNA RT-PCR (QUALITATIVE)",
  "code": "HCVQL",
  "cost": 0,
  "interpretation": "<p data-start=\"141\" data-end=\"165\"><strong data-start=\"145\" data-end=\"163\">About the Test</strong></p>\n<ul data-start=\"166\" data-end=\"403\">\n<li data-start=\"166\" data-end=\"239\">\n<p data-start=\"168\" data-end=\"239\">Detects the presence of <strong data-start=\"192\" data-end=\"223\">Hepatitis C virus (HCV) RNA</strong> in the blood.</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"240\" data-end=\"328\">\n<p data-start=\"242\" data-end=\"328\">Used to confirm <strong data-start=\"258\" data-end=\"278\">active infection</strong>, especially after a positive HCV antibody test.</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"329\" data-end=\"403\">\n<p data-start=\"331\" data-end=\"403\">More sensitive and specific than antibody tests for current infection.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th><strong>Result</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Meaning</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Clinical Significance</strong></th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Detected (Positive)</strong></td>\n<td>HCV RNA present in the blood.</td>\n<td>Confirms <strong>active HCV infection</strong> (acute or chronic). Requires further evaluation with <strong>HCV RNA quantitative PCR</strong> (viral load) and <strong>HCV genotype</strong> for treatment planning.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Not Detected (Negative)</strong></td>\n<td>No HCV RNA found.</td>\n<td>- No active infection. - May indicate <strong>resolved infection</strong> (spontaneous clearance or after treatment). - If patient had recent exposure (&le;6 weeks), repeat testing may be required due to window period.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Indeterminate / Invalid</strong></td>\n<td>Test could not give a conclusive result.</td>\n<td>Repeat testing recommended.</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<ul>\n<li>Clinical Significance</li>\n</ul>\n<ul>\n<li data-start=\"1203\" data-end=\"1307\">\n<p data-start=\"1205\" data-end=\"1307\"><strong data-start=\"1205\" data-end=\"1249\">Positive HCV antibody + Negative HCV RNA</strong> &rarr; past infection (resolved) or false-positive antibody.</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1308\" data-end=\"1380\">\n<p data-start=\"1310\" data-end=\"1380\"><strong data-start=\"1310\" data-end=\"1354\">Positive HCV antibody + Positive HCV RNA</strong> &rarr; <strong data-start=\"1357\" data-end=\"1377\">active infection</strong>.</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1381\" data-end=\"1555\">\n<p data-start=\"1383\" data-end=\"1555\">Test is <strong data-start=\"1391\" data-end=\"1411\">qualitative only</strong> &rarr; it tells presence or absence of virus, <strong data-start=\"1453\" data-end=\"1471\">not the amount</strong>. For monitoring and treatment response, <strong data-start=\"1512\" data-end=\"1540\">quantitative HCV RNA PCR</strong> is required.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>",
